	<element name="Disciple of Life" type="Archetype Feature" source="System Reference Document 5.1" id="ID_SRD_ARCHETYPE_FEATURE_LIFE_DOMAIN_DISCIPLE_OF_LIFE">
		<description><p>Whenever you use a spell of 1st level or higher to restore hit points to a creature, it regains additional hit points equal to 2 + the spell’s level.</p></description>
	</element>

	<element name="Channel Divinity: Preserve Life" type="Archetype Feature" source="System Reference Document 5.1" id="ID_SRD_ARCHETYPE_FEATURE_LIFE_DOMAIN_CHANNEL_DIVINITY_PRESERVE_LIFE">
		<description><p>As an action, you restore a number of hit points equal to five times your cleric level, divided as you choose among creatures within 30 feet. A creature can’t be restored above half its hit point maximum, and undead and constructs are unaffected.</p></description>
		<sheet>
			<description action="Action">Restore {{preserve life:hp}} hit points divided among creatures within 30 feet (up to half their maximum).</description>
		</sheet>
